66181.sol:
Let $C$ be the capacity of each capacitor. The equivalent capacitance of three capacitors in parallel combination will be $C_{p}=3 C$ and in series combination $C_{S}=\frac{C}{3}$
Let $V_{p}$ be the potential difference in parallel combination and $V_{S}$ in series combination then the energy stored in the same in the two cases. $\begin{array}{l}
\therefore\frac{1}{2}$ C_{p} V_p^{2}=$\frac{1}{2}$ C_{s} V_s^{2} \\
\therefore $\frac{V_p^{2}}{V_s^{2}}=\frac{C_{s}}{C_{p}}=\frac{C}{3} \cdot \frac{1}{3 C}=\frac{1}{9}$\\
\therefore $\frac{V_{p}}{V_{s}}=\frac{1}{3}
\end{array}$

